 Swipe keycodes are sent with `tap_code16()`, so modified keycodes work. For example, to switch macOS desktops the way a native trackpad does:
 
@@ -99,6 +105,8 @@ Swipe keycodes are sent with `tap_code16()`, so modified keycodes work. For exam
 
 With `DIGITIZER_MOUSE_PINCH_ENABLE`, nothing is sent while two fingers start moving. Once one of them has moved `DIGITIZER_TWO_FINGER_DECISION_DISTANCE`, the gesture is classified by the direction each finger moved: fingers moving in opposite directions (see `DIGITIZER_PINCH_OPPOSITE_COS_PERCENT`) whose distance also changed (see `DIGITIZER_PINCH_MIN_DISTANCE_CHANGE_PERCENT`) pinch; fingers moving the same way, or with one of them resting, scroll using their midpoint. The choice holds until the fingers lift or change, and the motion made before it is not lost. While pinching the modifiers are held (as weak mods) and spreading the fingers scrolls up, which zooms in with `Cmd`+scroll in apps such as Figma. Without `DIGITIZER_MOUSE_PINCH_ENABLE`, two fingers always scroll.
 
+With `DIGITIZER_MOUSE_EDGE_SWIPE_ENABLE`, two fingers whose midpoint starts within `DIGITIZER_EDGE_SWIPE_ZONE` of the left or right edge (for example, placed one above the other along the edge) send nothing while they move mostly inwards. Once the midpoint has moved `DIGITIZER_EDGE_SWIPE_DISTANCE` inwards, `DIGITIZER_EDGE_SWIPE_BACK_KC` (from the left edge) or `DIGITIZER_EDGE_SWIPE_FORWARD_KC` (from the right edge) is sent with `tap_code16()`, which is back and forward in macOS browsers by default. The rest of the gesture is then ignored until the fingers lift or change. If the fingers instead pinch, move outwards, move more vertically than inwards once they travelled `DIGITIZER_TWO_FINGER_DECISION_DISTANCE`, or move `DIGITIZER_EDGE_SWIPE_THRESHOLD` vertically, the gesture scrolls or pinches as usual and the motion made so far is not lost. Gestures that start outside the edge zones are not affected. The edges are measured in digitizer coordinates, so `digitizer_set_scale()` below 100% (without `DIGITIZER_MOUSE_CPI_POINTER_ONLY`) moves them inwards.
+
 ## Split Keyboard Configuration
 
 The following configuration options are only available when using `SPLIT_DIGITIZER_ENABLE` see [data sync options](split_keyboard#data-sync-options). If using `DIGITIZER_LEFT` or `DIGITIZER_RIGHT` use the common configuration above to configure your pointing device.
