@@ -23,6 +24,11 @@ moving in opposite directions (apart or together) pinch, fingers moving the same
 Resting one finger and moving the other scrolls, so pinch with both fingers. The choice holds
 until you lift your fingers, and nothing is lost while it is being made.
 
+For an edge swipe, put two fingers along the left or right edge (one above the other works best,
+their midpoint must start within about 6 mm of the edge) and swipe about 9 mm inwards. It fires
+once, then the gesture is ignored until you lift your fingers. Nothing scrolls while the swipe is
+undecided; moving up, down or outwards, or pinching, from the edge scrolls or pinches as usual.
+
 The tap, scroll, swipe and pinch thresholds are in `config.h`:
 
 | Define                                        | Default | Meaning                                                           |
